            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "John D"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Canned chili sauce for hot dogs rarely has any beef in it. Check the ingredients on the can. You are usually better off getting a can of chili without beans. If you take this recipe and add Cole slaw on the top you get what is known as a hot dog \"all the way\" in the Piedmont region of North Carolina.",
            "datePublished": "2025-06-30T18:04:50.522Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Paul Wright"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I'm from Detroit and the true chili sauce is purchased by the coneys from National Coney Island Company and is made from beef hearts. It sounds terrible, but tastes so good!",
            "datePublished": "2025-07-01T07:48:32.817Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CyanEel6024"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The hot dogs have to be Koegel's Viennas. A sliced-lengthwise, 1/4 Kosher Dill Pickle must be placed on top of each one. Bill Harper Linwood, MI",
            "datePublished": "2025-06-30T15:45:10.078Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "linda2d"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have missed these. I got a stash of sauce from one of the Detroit chains and used that instead of canned. These were a big hit during the Tiger game. Since I no longer eat hot dogs, making these at home with veggie dogs(I know, I know) is the only way I can enjoy them. Everyone else still has \"real\" hot dogs and enjoys these here as much as at the restaurant.",
            "datePublished": "2011-10-14T11:43:30.763Z"
